---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import Notice from '../components/Notice.astro';
import { hardware, photos, project } from '../data/project.js';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---
<SiteLayout title="Hardware and printable cases" description="Explore the Corney Choc and MX builds, printable sources, optional Cirque trackpads, and SSD1306 dongle OLED wiring." current="build">
  <div class="shell page-hero"><span class="eyebrow">Hardware / build your own</span><h1>Pick your feel.<br />Shape your desk.</h1><p class="lead">Corney's repository contains printable case sources for low-profile Choc and MX builds. Pointing and the dongle display are optional additions to the firmware topology.</p></div>
  <section class="shell section variants" aria-labelledby="variants-title"><div class="section-intro"><span class="eyebrow">Two physical expressions</span><h2 id="variants-title">Choc or MX</h2><p>The printable sources are in the repository. Check the geometry and switch/PCB fit of your own parts before printing.</p></div><div class="grid-2"><article class="variant"><img src={photos.choc.src} alt={photos.choc.alt} width="750" height="320" /><div><span class="eyebrow">01 / low profile</span><h3>Choc</h3><p>Compact enclosure and plate sources for the low-profile Corne Chocoflan remix, including trackpad-related parts.</p><a class="text-link" href={project.printable.choc}>Browse Choc sources ↗</a></div></article><article class="variant"><img src={photos.mx.src} alt={photos.mx.alt} width="750" height="568" /><div><span class="eyebrow">02 / classic feel</span><h3>MX</h3><p>Printable body and cover sources for MX switches and taller keycaps.</p><a class="text-link" href={project.printable.mx}>Browse MX sources ↗</a></div></article></div></section>
  <section class="shell section"><div class="section-intro"><span class="eyebrow">Optional pointing</span><h2>A trackpad where it helps.</h2><p>Each half can host its own Cirque Pinnacle sensor on its Pro Micro I²C pins. The same half firmware works when a sensor is absent.</p></div><div class="grid-3"><div class="card"><span class="card-number">01 / LEFT</span><h3>Local or remote</h3><p>In Direct Bluetooth mode, the left sensor is local to the central. In USB Dongle mode it forwards movement over the split link.</p></div><div class="card"><span class="card-number">02 / RIGHT</span><h3>Remote pointing</h3><p>The right half forwards relative movement, tap and wheel input to whichever central is active.</p></div><div class="card"><span class="card-number">03 / POWER</span><h3>Wake with a key</h3><p>The sensor is polled while active. Trackpad touch alone cannot wake a sleeping half without its data-ready connection.</p></div></div><Notice title="Pointing has a physical boundary"><p>A sensor replaces the former OLED position on a half. The dongle has no physical trackpad. Simultaneously holding the same mouse button on both sensors is unsupported.</p></Notice></section>
  <section class="shell section oled" id="oled"><div><span class="eyebrow">USB dongle / display</span><h2>Status at a glance.</h2><p>A dedicated {hardware.controller} dongle can drive a four-wire {hardware.display} panel. Its screen keeps output status at the upper left and local battery at the upper right. Two remote battery readings appear as one unlabeled pair under the local indicator, and the bottom row shows the full active layer name beside a keyboard symbol.</p><p class="small">Remote battery values follow split connection slot order and do not identify the physical left or right half. Long layer names scroll slowly through the available bottom-row window.</p><a class="text-link" href={`${base}/guide/#oled`}>Understand display states ↗</a></div><div class="oled-card" role="img" aria-label="Diagram of the dongle OLED with output at upper left, local battery at upper right, two remote percentages beneath it, and a scrolling active layer name along the bottom row"><div><span>USB</span><span>▰ 84%</span></div><div><span></span><span>78% 56%</span></div><div><span>⌨ MAC: Characters</span><span></span></div></div></section>
  <section class="shell section"><div class="section-intro"><span class="eyebrow">OLED wiring</span><h2>Four connections to the dongle.</h2><p>Connect the display to the dedicated dongle controller only. The halves' I²C buses remain available for optional trackpads.</p></div><div class="wiring" role="table" aria-label="SSD1306 to nice nano v2 wiring"><div role="row"><strong role="columnheader">SSD1306</strong><strong role="columnheader">Dongle {hardware.controller}</strong></div><div role="row"><span role="cell">VCC</span><span role="cell">3V3</span></div><div role="row"><span role="cell">GND</span><span role="cell">GND</span></div><div role="row"><span role="cell">SDA</span><span role="cell">D2 / P0.17</span></div><div role="row"><span role="cell">SCL</span><span role="cell">D3 / P0.20</span></div></div><Notice title="Use a 3.3 V compatible panel." tone="warning"><p>The firmware expects a 128 × 64 SSD1306 at address <code>0x3c</code>. Do not connect an unknown panel to RAW or 5 V.</p></Notice></section>
  <section class="shell section" id="dongle-case"><div class="section-intro"><span class="eyebrow">USB dongle / prototype case</span><h2>A printable shell for the dongle.</h2><p>The repository includes a prototype case for the dongle: a bottom shell, an upper shell with USB, screen and reset-button openings, and a small reset button. It is designed around a 30 × 70 mm breadboard, so it suits hobbyists who are comfortable printing, testing and adjusting their own parts.</p></div><Notice title="Prototype: adjust before you print." tone="warning"><p>The board size, inner height and wall thickness are parameters at the top of the OpenSCAD file, and the screen cut-out is still being refined. Check the fit against your own controller and display, and change the parameters if they differ.</p></Notice><div class="btn-row"><a class="btn btn-outline" href={`${base}/models/`}>Preview the dongle case ↗</a><a class="btn btn-outline" href={`${project.repository}/tree/main/body/dongle`}>Browse OpenSCAD sources ↗</a></div></section>
  <section class="shell section"><div class="source-panel"><div><span class="eyebrow">Keep exploring</span><h2>Sources, keymap and firmware.</h2><p>All printable files, the ZMK keymap and firmware configuration live in the Corney repository.</p></div><div class="source-links"><a href={`${base}/models/`}>Preview 3D models ↗</a><a href={project.docs.keymap}>View keymap ↗</a><a href={project.repository}>Open source repository ↗</a><a href={`${base}/firmware/`}>Choose firmware ↗</a></div></div></section>
</SiteLayout>

<style>
.variant{background:var(--panel);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:12px;overflow:hidden}.variant img{width:100%;height:280px;object-fit:cover}.variant>div{padding:26px}.variant h3{font-size:1.8rem;margin:10px 0}.variant p{color:var(--muted);min-height:60px}.oled{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1fr;align-items:center;gap:80px}.oled p{color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7}.oled-card{background:#020608;border:17px solid #2b3135;outline:2px solid #687b7b;border-radius:20px;box-shadow:16px 20px 0 #19262b;width:min(100%,420px);aspect-ratio:2;display:flex;flex-direction:column;justify-content:space-between;padding:19px 23px;font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;color:#e6eee9;font-size:clamp(.85rem,1.6vw,1.3rem)}.oled-card>div{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:10px}.wiring{max-width:700px;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:8px;overflow:hidden}.wiring>div{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;padding:12px 18px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);gap:12px}.wiring>div:first-child{background:var(--panel2);color:var(--accent)}.wiring>div:last-child{border-bottom:0}.wiring>div:nth-child(odd):not(:first-child){background:var(--panel)}.source-panel{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:30px;align-items:center;background:var(--panel);padding:35px;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:12px}.source-panel p{color:var(--muted);margin-bottom:0}.source-panel h2{font-size:2rem;margin:10px 0}.source-links{display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:flex-start;gap:10px;flex-shrink:0}.source-links a{color:var(--accent);font-weight:700;text-decoration:none}.source-links a:hover{text-decoration:underline}
@media(max-width:800px){.oled{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:35px}.oled-card{box-shadow:none}.variant img{height:220px}.source-panel{align-items:flex-start;flex-direction:column}}
@media(max-width:600px){.variant p{min-height:0}.oled-card{border-width:10px;padding:12px;font-size:.8rem}}
</style>
